  "body": "### Summary\nTwo late CodeRabbit findings on #700 (LOT-118 follow-up, #687), deferred because the PR had reached its CodeRabbit round cap (2 rounds, operator rule). Low risk; fix together in one small PR.\n\n### Scope\n1. **Minor.** `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/PseudoListEditorModel.swift:86` (head 2f1fca2): `add()` reads `draft` before awaiting `settleRemovals()`; text the user types during that wait is lost or the older text is submitted. Read and clear `draft` consistently after the wait (or capture it once and keep the newer edit). Test: an edit during the wait is kept. Thread: https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/700#discussion_r4517774290\n2. **Trivial.** `App/SwiftHFRTests/PseudoLists/PseudoListTests.swift:240`: test-structure suggestion from CodeRabbit (https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/700#discussion_r4517774299). Apply only if it simplifies.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Swift Testing test for item 1, shown to fail without the fix.\n- Mac check not needed beyond CI.\n\nM4. Origin: swift-feedback.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
